 test consists of 15 multiple-choice questions covering Indian road signs, traffic signals, and fundamental driving regulations. You must answer at least 11 questions correctly (60% score) within the allotted 30 seconds per question to pass.","displayOrder":0,"status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://sarathi.parivahan.gov.in"},{"question":"When can I apply for a permanent driving licence after getting my learner licence?","answer":"You can apply for a permanent driving licence after 30 days from your Learner Licence issue date. You must apply within 180 days (6 months) before the learner licence expires.","displayOrder":0,"status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://morth.nic.in"}],"rejectionReasons":[{"title":"Name or Date of Birth Mismatch on Aadhaar","description":"If the name on your 10th marksheet or birth certificate does not match the name returned by Aadhaar e-KYC, the application is halted.","solution":"Update your Aadhaar details first at an Aadhaar Seva Kendra, or apply via non-Aadhaar mode with physical document scrutiny at the RTO.","status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://sarathi.parivahan.gov.in"}],"sourceRefs":[{"title":"The Motor Vehicles (Amendment) Act, 2019","actOrRuleNumber":"Section 8 and 9","issuingAuthority":"Parliament of India / MoRTH","url":"https://morth.nic.in","status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z"}],"taskSlug":"driving-licence-learner","taskName":"Learner's Licence Application","categorySlug":"vehicles","categoryName":"Vehicles and Driving","isStateOverride":false,"stateCode":"TG","stateName":"Telangana","stateSlug":"telangana","launchState":"$undefined"},"relatedTasks":[{"slug":"driving-licence-new","name":"Permanent Driving Licence Application","description":"How to get a permanent driving licence in India after holding a learner permit, with automated test track steps and Gujarat state rules.","categorySlug":"vehicles","categoryName":"Vehicles and Driving","difficulty":"medium","estimatedTime":"15-30 days after driving test","cost":"₹200 – ₹300","availableStates":["GJ"]}],"popularTasks":[{"slug":"driving-licence-learner","name":"Learner's Licence Application","description":"How to apply for a learner driving licence (LLR) online or at an RTO in India.","categorySlug":"vehicles","categoryName":"Vehicles and Driving","difficulty":"easy","estimatedTime":"15-30 days","cost":"₹50 – ₹150","availableStates":["GJ"]},{"slug":"driving-licence-new","name":"Permanent Driving Licence Application","description":"How to get a permanent driving licence in India after holding a learner permit, with automated test track steps and Gujarat state rules.","categorySlug":"vehicles","categoryName":"Vehicles and Driving","difficulty":"medium","estimatedTime":"15-30 days after driving test","cost":"₹200 – ₹300","availableStates":["GJ"]},{"slug":"passport-renewal","name":"Passport Renewal (Re-issue)","description":"Complete guide to renewing or re-issuing an Indian passport online with verified fees, document checklist, and PSK appointment steps.","categorySlug":"identity","categoryName":"Identity Documents","difficulty":"medium","estimatedTime":"7-14 working days (Normal) / 1-3 days (Tatkaal)","cost":"₹1,500 – ₹2,000","availableStates":[]},{"slug":"pan-card-new","name":"New PAN Card (Form 49A)","description":"Apply for a new Permanent Account Number online or via physical application.","categorySlug":"money-and-tax","categoryName":"Money and Tax","difficulty":"easy","estimatedTime":"10–15 days","cost":"₹107","availableStates":[]}],"state":{"name":"Telangana","nativeName":"తెలంగాణ","slug":"telangana","code":"TG","primaryLanguages":["te","en","ur"],"portalName":"MeeSeva Telangana","portalUrl":""},"isStatePage":true}]
